{"authored" [{"question" "q-125485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $25{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25$ oriented counterclockwise. Interpret circulation as the sum of four convergent improper line integrals over the open quadrant arcs, with independent one-sided limits at $(\\pm1,0)$ and $(0,\\pm5)$. The field is undefined at those four points, so the original ordinary circulation is not defined." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/review.json" "file_sha256" "fcd625007a9cfee7b096a716cd4de8cfead25f34afa8ad5af2e15973d46de245" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d012cceeac9e1ea0bb534095f2bc255ab19c76007b69cab4d0fad20ac04f4ee8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/verification.json" "basis" 1940 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield 8pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The original field is undefined at the four axis intersections, so an ordinary line integral over the whole ellipse is not defined. For the explicit improper interpretation, $r(t)=(\\cos t,5\\sin t)$ traverses $25x^2+y^2=25$ counterclockwise. On each open quadrant arc,\n\n$$\\frac{5}{y}\\,dx=\\frac{5}{5\\sin t}(-\\sin t)\\,dt=-dt,\\qquad\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy=\\frac{1}{\\cos t}(5\\cos t)\\,dt=5dt.$$\n\nThus the scalar pullback is $4$. Each endpoint has the finite one-sided limit $4$, so each open-arc integral converges absolutely and equals $2\\pi$. Their sum is $\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{imp}}=8\\pi$, the unchanged option c. No principal-value cancellation is used, and $F$ remains undefined at the excluded points." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/review.json" "file_sha256" "fcd625007a9cfee7b096a716cd4de8cfead25f34afa8ad5af2e15973d46de245" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d012cceeac9e1ea0bb534095f2bc255ab19c76007b69cab4d0fad20ac04f4ee8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/verification.json" "basis" 1940 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield 8pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8π"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/review.json" "file_sha256" "fcd625007a9cfee7b096a716cd4de8cfead25f34afa8ad5af2e15973d46de245" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "d012cceeac9e1ea0bb534095f2bc255ab19c76007b69cab4d0fad20ac04f4ee8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125485/verification.json" "basis" 1940 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield 8pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $25{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25$ oriented counterclockwise." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $1$ and $5,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1+5 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =4(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =8\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0739c96ad346238c47110cc19d8571d34c4c37477e99709f7d89249005e6827" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_s